{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794318111713,"sessionID":"ses_e3a6c3a5fffeccW8fg8yb88t39","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_1049428a86104abf9a32ae25","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -la /workspace; cat /workspace/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -50"},"output":"total 56\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:27 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Nov 10 13:09 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node 12103 Nov 10 13:21 .api_test.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   118 Jan  1  1970 .dockerignore\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:28 .git\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   393 Nov 10 13:27 .gunicorn.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node     6 Nov 10 13:27 .server.pid\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  1062 Jan  1  1970 Dockerfile\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   887 Jan  1  1970 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:14 backend\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:41 data\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:34 frontend\n# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n","metadata":{"output":"total 56\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:27 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Nov 10 13:09 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node 12103 Nov 10 13:21 .api_test.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   118 Jan  1  1970 .dockerignore\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:28 .git\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   393 Nov 10 13:27 .gunicorn.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node     6 Nov 10 13:27 .server.pid\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  1062 Jan  1  1970 Dockerfile\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   887 Jan  1  1970 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:14 backend\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:41 data\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 node node  4096 Nov 10 13:34 frontend\n# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls -la /workspace; cat /workspace/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -50","time":{"start":1794318111684,"end":1794318111710}},"id":"prt_1c5b193bf001HKY79ivB321qq1","sessionID":"ses_e3a6c3a5fffeccW8fg8yb88t39","messageID":"msg_1c5b0ee29001l7BY3WXvL6I2kO"}}
